  "prerequisites": [],
  "story": "A factory stamps codes that have no prime factors other than 2, 3 and 5: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 12 and so on (7 and 14 are skipped). What is the n-th code? For n up to 1500 the codes reach the hundreds of millions, so testing every number in turn takes far too long. Every code after 1 is a smaller code times 2, 3 or 5.",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "n", "type": "num"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {"notes": ["n is 1 to 1500."]},
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.add", "arith.floor_div", "arith.mod", "arith.mul", "cmp.eq", "cmp.lt", "ctrl.for_range", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "ctrl.while", "heap.empty", "heap.insert", "heap.size", "heap.take", "heap.top", "lit.num", "logic.not", "new.max_heap", "new.min_heap", "new.set", "set.add", "set.has", "var.get", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 111
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 111700, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 4350},
  "performance": {"required": true, "baselineFactor": 10},
  "hints": ["Start a NEW MIN HEAP with 1 in it. TAKE TOP n times: the n-th number taken is the answer.", "Each time you take a code x, INSERT x TIMES 2, x TIMES 3 and x TIMES 5: they are codes too, and larger.", "The same code can be made twice (6 is 2 × 3 and 3 × 2). Keep a NEW SET of codes already put in, and INSERT one only IF the set does NOT HAS it."],
